      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a predictive risk model for residential property theft in the Greater Metro area. I'm looking through some recent census data and local crime stats for the 90210 and surrounding ZIPs. I've noticed some significant shifts in the demographic makeup and ethnic composition of these neighborhoods over the last 5 years. From an actuarial standpoint, how much weight should I be giving to these changes in ethnic/racial diversity when trying to predict larceny and theft trends? I want to see if there's a statistically significant correlation there for our underwriting models.",
